## 8. Test-runner Fast-Fail Configuration (dis-core)

dis-core-specific tooling and Copilot-run tests must honor the workspace-wide
fast-fail probe settings to prevent long freezes during automated or iterative
validation. These settings are required for all Copilot-driven quick-runs and
test scaffolding inside this repository.

Local rules:
- probe_timeout_ms: 300
- retry_backoff: false
- surface_errors_immediately: true
- fail_on_non_json: true

Apply these when generating test code, harnesses, or helper scripts that probe
HTTP endpoints (including internal admin endpoints like bootstrap or policy
validation). Treat interactive prompts as failures in automated contexts and
report them immediately.
No free-form architecture. No spontaneous new paradigms.
